<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="76807" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HK/594/76807.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="HK" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HK.xml">Health and Kinesiology</subject><course id="594" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HK/594.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>HA </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Health Administration</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Foundations of Epidemiology and Biostatics in Health Administration.  The goal of this 16-week course is to introduce the basic concepts and principles of epidemiology and biostatistics. The course is formatted to include two weekly lectures and a weekly lab session, with the first 8 weeks devoted to epidemiology and the second 8 weeks devoted to biostatistics. Lectures will introduce students to key epidemiologic principles and basic biostatistical approaches. The lab will reinforce these concepts by allowing students to work on problem sets, case studies, data management, and hypothesis testing.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Health Administration major(s).</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>166</roomNumber><buildingName>Education Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Amaral de Andrade Leao" firstName="O">Amaral de Andrade Leao, O</instructor><instructor lastName="Barnes" firstName="B">Barnes, B</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>